WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.975
Bring a ride video along. Wattzup keeps it in step with your ride.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.182
Below the plan, turn on Ride along to a video. It plays in sync on the dashboard.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.049
Paste a YouTube link. Anything else is named: that doesn't look like a YouTube link.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.292
Scrub the preview past the intro, and set where ride zero starts: twelve seconds in.

00:00:33.492 --> 00:00:37.119
The preview adds a line: Video, synced from twelve seconds.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.501
On the dashboard, the video takes the main view, with the plan strip beneath it.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:47.228
A second tab holds Power versus plan.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.684
Pause the video, and the ride pauses with it. Resume one, and both carry on.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.600
On a phone, the video sits under the numbers.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.453
What the tests prove: if the video drifts more than a second and a half, it seeks

00:01:14.453 --> 00:01:15.687
back to the ride.

00:01:15.887 --> 00:01:18.931
And whenever the ride isn't running, the video holds.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.490
That is journey nine. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.794
training display.
